# The callback of a bundler's wrapper that runs it once is the body of a module of its own, written in the text of a file: `function f1 module=m0`, the body of m1. The body of the file makes the wrapper: where the loader enters that body at most once, it enters the callback at most once, and so whatever the callback alone calls once.
# main.js: var load = wrap(() => { once() });  load();  function once() { return 1 }
